{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1108687-how-different-are-1st-and-2nd-edition-nwod-cofd","id":1108687,"title":"How different are 1st and 2nd edition nWoD/CofD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-28T03:53:19-07:00","id":1108687,"title":"How different are 1st and 2nd edition nWoD/CofD?","content":"I got the new Chronicle of Darkness book and really liked it, and really want to GM or play it, but I have a... problem.<br /> <br /> Some of the splats I am more interested lack a 2nd edition book (Mummies, Changeling, although Changeling is supposed to get a 2nd edition book this year, right?). How has the system changed? If I get a 1st edition splat for a 2nd edition game, it will be literally unplayable? It is hard to convert? Easy? Conditions are new, right? It\u00b4s that the biggest change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T05:47:23-07:00","id":1108719,"title":"","content":"The conversion is usually pretty easy - a few rules changes, and clarifications (Conditions are usually the old &quot;X happens for this long&quot; effects, but encapsulated into something discrete. You can print out the common ones or write in note cards instead of having to remember all persistent effects.) Weapons, Morality, Virtue/Vice, Defense, Armor, and Ephemeral Entities are the most noticeable change areas.<br /> <br /> Changeling 2E is in development, but the Playtest doc released should get you close.<br /> Geist and Mummy likely require a bit more work due to the mechanics they interface with (Ephemeral Entities and Virtue/Vices, respectively), bit there are many good Conversions on the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T13:17:16-07:00","id":1108908,"title":"","content":"Flat xp instead of exponential. For example a merit costs 1 xp per dot not 1xp x new dots. Of course this requires a scaling back of xp gain but the beat system hands more power to the players in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Weapon damage is the base damage done instead of just bonus dice. Athletics adds to defence.<br /> <br /> Most things done though are in the GMC free update if you are curious. The CofD core has some additional things but more its nice to not have to reference 2 books while ignoring 'half' of one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T14:31:47-07:00","id":1108943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1108687-how-different-are-1st-and-2nd-edition-nwod-cofd?p=1108908#post1108908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flat xp instead of exponential. For example a merit costs 1 xp per dot not 1xp x new dots. Of course this requires a scaling back of xp gain but the beat system hands more power to the players in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Weapon damage is the base damage done instead of just bonus dice. Athletics adds to defence.<br /> <br /> Most things done though are in the GMC free update if you are curious. The CofD core has some additional things but more its nice to not have to reference 2 books while ignoring 'half' of one</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it can be a bit hard to find, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">here is the link to the free update</a>. Beast also has some guidelines on how to update splats to 2e if you want to feature them in a game. The <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/170165/Demon-Storytellers-Guide?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Storyteller's Guide </a>and <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/214130/Thousand-Years-of-Night?term=Thousand+Years?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Thousand Years of Night</a> both offer suggestions of how to model all other splats using the preexisting rules of Demon and Vampire respectively. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}